## Michael's Memo: "How Fast Can I Get Funding?"

When we hear that question, we know exactly what's happening.

There's pressure. A payroll deadline looming. A time-sensitive opportunity to close a new customer. A new contract or project that needs to get moving. Inventory that has to be purchased ahead of a critical season.

We get it. Yet the key dynamics of a capital facility are much like a three-legged stool: speed, cost, and quality.

You can get money fast. But will it fuel growth, or create stress you can't outrun?

Cheaper money usually takes more time. Fast money usually costs more. And quality? That's all about the structure of the deal. Payments that respect cash flow. Capital that helps a business breathe instead of choke.

So when a business owner asks, "How fast can I get funding?", the better question is: what am I willing to give up for that speed?

Sometimes speed is the main priority. And sometimes a little extra patience now saves months, or years, of pain later. Because it's not just about fast money. It's about smart money. And that's where sound advice actually matters.

Here to serve,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: Smart Speed Under Pressure, $300K Funded in Days

A high-end corporate and wedding event venue does 60 to 70% of its annual volume in the last three months of the year. Strong demand, but heavy seasonal strain on cash flow, and a planned sale on the horizon. The client's bank held an all-asset senior lien and had to decline additional credit because of historical losses, a byproduct of seasonality and high fixed costs rather than operational weakness.

Serve Funding secured a $300,000 term loan for seasonal working capital in under one week: a 22-month term with steady payments, and 100% of remaining interest waived as an option on prepayment. Immediate relief, and a clean runway to exit the facility once cash flow normalized.

The full story is in the case study: [$300K for an Event Venue, With a Clean Exit](/blog/event-venue-seasonal-working-capital).

{% callout type="tip" title="The takeaway" %}
When a business owner asks how fast, the right answer isn't just a timeline. It's a structure that works today and doesn't punish them tomorrow. That's the difference between fast money and smart money.
{% /callout %}

